      "q": "Handoff §3 design notes say the breaker 'should also consider whether the same root cause recurs' (in addition to whether blockers are decreasing and whether new material genuinely requires another round) — does this require the stall gate to track root-cause identity/recurrence as a distinct signal beyond the existing STALL_WINDOW non-improving blocking-count trend that CHK-001 reuses, or is reusing the existing trend signal sufficient to satisfy this design note?",
      "evidence": "\"A raw absolute cap alone is too crude — the breaker should also consider whether blockers are decreasing, whether the same root cause recurs, and whether new material genuinely requires another round.\" (docs/step3-review-budget-breaker-handoff.md §3). CHK-001's context and verificationIntent only reuse the existing STALL_MIN_ROUNDS/STALL_WINDOW blocking-count trend (\"Reuses the existing assessReviewConvergence trend logic\"); no checklist item or plan.md section mentions tracking root-cause identity across rounds as a separate signal.",
